          "path": "_m/e/z/j/m/siege-of-madrid-wp/portada-la-traca-24-de-febrer-.jpg",
          "filename": "Portada La Traca - 24 de febrer del 1937.jpg",
          "caption": "Cover of the satirical magazine La Traca during the Spanish Civil War, in which a caricature of two nationalist soldiers belonging to the Army of Africa is shown. In it they are represented with the stereotypical attributes of the black African people according to the western vision of the time, with large red lips and googly eyes. The image is accompanied by a text that says the following:\nNegroes in the front of Madrid, by Bluff.\nAnd whoever calls me Kaffir from now on, I kill him! Until I saw a fascist I did not know what a Kaffir was.",
          "alt": "Cover of the satirical magazine La Traca during the Spanish Civil War, in which a caricature of two nationalist soldiers belonging to the Army of Africa is shown. In it they are represented with the stereotypical attributes of the black African people according to the western vision of the time, with large red lips and googly eyes. The image is accompanied by a text that says the following:\nNegroes in the front of Madrid, by Bluff.\nAnd whoever calls me Kaffir from now on, I kill him! Until I saw a fascist I did not know what a Kaffir was.",
          "width": 1694,
          "height": 2483,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "Public domain",
          "artist": "Carlos Gómez Carrera",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portada_La_Traca_-_24_de_febrer_del_1937.jpg",
